{
  "case_id": "2019-18-938",
  "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEHMAN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: 28 U.S.C. Section 158 provides that district courts shall have jurisdiction to hear appeals from final order of bankruptcy judges entered in cases and proceedings referred to bankruptcy judges under Section 157. The order in this case merely determined where the parties would litigate Ritzen's contract claim. Under Section 158, such an order is not a final order entered in a case or proceeding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But, as I understand what you've just said, you're not contesting that this was a proceeding. You're just saying it wasn't a final order in the proceeding. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "By objecting as an informal proof of claim, the Respondent is triggering the entire claims adjudication process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0001-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We filed an adversarial proceeding. They filed an adversarial proceeding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Your theory under the Bullard test is that the denial of relief from the stay does not alter the status quo for the creditor, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When the rules changed in 1984 from 701 to 7001, challenges to stays no longer were raised as adversarial proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: How do we balance"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: They argue from the language in Bullard that the -- the \"alter the status quo\" language in Bullard that this doesn't -- the denial here doesn't meet that test. Can you address that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0002-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SURI: It is not just the bankruptcy judge's equitable sense. And the best way to see that is in Section 362(e) where Congress repeatedly uses the word \"final\" to determine -- to refer to a bankruptcy judge's determination of a stay relief order."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Suri, may I take you to a different place? MR. SURI: Yes. JUSTICE KAGAN: In the last page of your brief, you refer to another circuit split. Apparently, there are some circuits that say, although you may bring an appeal immediately, you don't have to and you can wait until the end."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, the Respondents actually cited a case to the Court that changed that. On page 38 of their brief, the Gledhill case from the Tenth Circuit actually granted relief from stay and 10 months later then reconsidered and changed that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the Respondent and the government continue to ignore the fact that 362(e) relates only to actions against the property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-938",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d55ed32db7e697e84c243fb109f5d49eca330dc6f14011bdbb859cfc2699c2f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d55ed32db7e-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:10 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
